From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:43:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Pass the check-run data to curl through stdin

With hundreds of unexpected results, the check-run summary exceeds the
argument size limit, and "Report results" failed with "OSError: [Errno 7]
Argument list too long: 'curl'" (QuickJS WPT run of 2026-10-10).

Validation: the same subprocess call delivered a 3 MB body to a local HTTP server; the step itself only runs in CI.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which found the cause in the run's log)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 etc/ci/report_aggregated_expected_results.py | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/etc/ci/report_aggregated_expected_results.py b/etc/ci/report_aggregated_expected_results.py
index 13dd03e049b..a355ea82670 100755
--- a/etc/ci/report_aggregated_expected_results.py
+++ b/etc/ci/report_aggregated_expected_results.py
@@ -235,7 +235,8 @@ def create_github_reports(body: str, tag: str = ""):
         "actions": [],
     }
 
-    subprocess.Popen(
+    # The data goes through stdin: with many unexpected results, it exceeds the argument size limit.
+    subprocess.run(
         [
             "curl",
             "-L",
@@ -249,9 +250,11 @@ def create_github_reports(body: str, tag: str = ""):
             "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28",
             f"https://api.github.com/repos/{repo}/check-runs",
             "-d",
-            json.dumps(data),
-        ]
-    ).wait()
+            "@-",
+        ],
+        input=json.dumps(data),
+        text=True,
+    )
 
 
 def main():
